  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nElections - Woodbury County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n Skip to content\n \n\n \n\n \n Woodbury County\n Iowa • Elections\n \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n \n\n \n \nVote \n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections \n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials \n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \nDrainage\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n Woodbury County\nElections\n\n\n\n Due to staffing and security needs, the ballot drop box is no longer in use. Voted ballots can be returned by mail or in person to 620 Douglas St, Rm 103. Other Election News & Satellite Locations \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nWelcome to the Woodbury County Elections Website.\n The Auditor's Office is responsible for every aspect of conducting an election from voter registration to the final count of the votes. This site is designed to be a resource for residents looking to learn how to vote, find their elected officials, learn about becoming a candidate, or find past or upcoming election information.\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \nQuick Links\n \nRegister to Vote\n \nWhere Do I Vote?\n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nAm I Registered?\n \nHow Do I Vote?\n \nWhere's My Absentee Ballot?\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nUpcoming & Recent Elections\n \n\n \n\n \nSep\n \n8\n \n \n\n 2026 Kingsley-Pierson Community School Special Election\n Special Election\n \n\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nSep\n \n8\n \n \n\n 2026 Maple Valley-Anthon Oto Community School Special Election\n Special Election\n \n\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nAug\n \n18\n \n \n\n 2026 City of Salix Special Election\n Special Election\n \n\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n News\n \n\n 2026 Satellite Location Press Release\n \n September 22, 2026 Woodbury County Announces Satellite In-Person Voting Locations for the 2026 General Election \n\n\n\n\n 2026 Public Measure 1: Constitutional Amendment - Full Language\n \n October 12, 2026 Ballots will show the Summary of the Statewide Constitutional Amendment. Review full language here. \n\n\n\nAll News\n \n \n\n \n FAQ\n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nI lost my absentee ballot; can I just go vote on Election Day?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nYes. When you go to vote, a poll worker will verify with the auditor’s office that your absentee ballot has not been returned. If it is confirmed that the auditor’s office has not received a ballot from you then you will be given a new ballot to vote there. \n\n \n\n \n \nAll Frequently Asked Questions\n \n \n\n \n Woodbury County Voter Registration\n \n\n Updated September 22, 2026\n \n\n\n \nRepublican\n \n\n\n \n23,321\n \n\n \nNo Party\n \n\n\n \n20,513\n \n\n \nDemocratic\n \n\n\n \n16,118\n \n\n \nOther\n \n\n\n \n508\n \n\n \n \n \nTotal Registered Voters: 60,460\n \n Register to Vote\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\nThis webpage was printed on October 17, 2026. For the most current election-related information, visit the Woodbury County, Iowa, Elections website at https://elections.woodburycountyiowa.gov.\n\n\n\n \n\n Woodbury County Courthouse\n\n 620 Douglas St. - Room 103\n \nSioux City, IA 51101\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n Woodbury County Website\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n Monday - Friday\n \n8AM - 4:30PM \n \nContact Information\n\n Phone: (712) 279-6465\n \nFax: (712) 2796629 \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n"
